WEBVTT

00:03.828 --> 00:05.829
Ugh.

00:05.831 --> 00:07.330
How is it possible

00:07.332 --> 00:10.367
that kids weigh twice as
much when they're asleep?

00:10.369 --> 00:11.668
I know.

00:11.670 --> 00:13.703
And he should weigh less
after his little mishap

00:13.705 --> 00:15.271
on the spinning teacups.

00:15.273 --> 00:17.207
Yeah.

00:17.209 --> 00:19.609
Felt bad for that girl
in the Cinderella costume

00:19.611 --> 00:21.444
in the cup behind us.

00:21.446 --> 00:24.447
She was right in
the splash zone.

00:24.449 --> 00:26.483
(groans)
I'm exhausted.

00:26.485 --> 00:28.118
Me, too.

00:28.120 --> 00:31.121
I'm also sticky and dirty
and sweaty and slimy.

00:31.123 --> 00:34.391
I'm like the seven dwarfs
of disgusting.

00:34.393 --> 00:37.160
Ugh, I should not have eaten
that funnel cake.

00:37.162 --> 00:38.628
(groans)

00:38.630 --> 00:40.296
Well, I see
your funnel cake

00:40.298 --> 00:44.401
and raise you a deep-fried
Snickers stuffed into a Twinkie.

00:44.403 --> 00:47.337
I think I blacked out briefly.

00:47.339 --> 00:49.506
(both groaning)

00:51.075 --> 00:53.943
Is being a dad always
this tiring?

00:53.945 --> 00:57.614
These are the best
moments of your life.

00:57.616 --> 01:00.350
And they are over
so fast.

01:00.352 --> 01:02.252
Seems like only yesterday,

01:02.254 --> 01:05.622
Jake was holding my hand
in the haunted house.

01:05.624 --> 01:09.259
Now he's half a world away
in the army,

01:09.261 --> 01:12.295
wondering if a "dishonorable
discharge" is something you get

01:12.297 --> 01:13.696
from a dirty geisha.

01:13.698 --> 01:15.899
So sweet.

01:23.507 --> 01:26.309
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

01:26.311 --> 01:28.236
♪ Ah. ♪
♪ Men. ♪

01:28.237 --> 01:32.237
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 12x07 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">Sex With an Animated Ed Asner&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on December 11, 2014

01:32.238 --> 01:36.238
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>

01:36.239 --> 01:39.007
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

01:39.009 --> 01:40.175
Walden?

01:40.177 --> 01:43.178
What?

01:44.247 --> 01:45.447
What do you want?

01:45.449 --> 01:46.815
Are you asleep?

01:46.817 --> 01:49.618
(whines): 3Ks.

01:49.620 --> 01:52.921
That's what people do at...

01:52.923 --> 01:56.458
5:30 in the morning.

01:56.460 --> 01:58.994
Is it okay
if I can make breakfast?

01:58.996 --> 02:00.262
Sure.

02:00.264 --> 02:01.763
Thanks.

02:04.901 --> 02:06.067
Walden?

02:06.069 --> 02:10.105
Walden's not here,
please leave a message.

02:10.107 --> 02:12.407
How do you like your pancakes?

02:12.409 --> 02:14.409
Quietly.

02:14.411 --> 02:17.712
In three hours.

02:17.714 --> 02:20.081
With blueberries.

02:20.083 --> 02:22.017
Okay, I'll go make them.

02:25.555 --> 02:27.055
Oh, God.

02:27.057 --> 02:29.591
Flames.

02:29.593 --> 02:31.726
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

02:31.728 --> 02:33.628
Walden?

02:33.630 --> 02:35.597
Ready or not, here I come.

02:35.599 --> 02:37.465
What?

02:37.467 --> 02:40.035
Louis and I,
we're playing hide and seek.

02:40.037 --> 02:41.803
He's under his bed, hiding

02:41.805 --> 02:44.773
and I'm in the kitchen,
seeking sleep.

02:44.775 --> 02:46.441
I hear ya.

02:46.443 --> 02:49.044
I barely got my eight hours.

02:49.046 --> 02:50.946
I don't know
if I can handle this.

02:50.948 --> 02:52.914
Little boys have
a lot of energy.

02:52.916 --> 02:54.482
They're like cute
little crackheads.

02:54.484 --> 02:57.586
Except crackheads have
better toilet aim.

02:57.588 --> 02:59.888
No, no, this isn't about
being tired.

02:59.890 --> 03:02.857
I just, I don't know
if I'm cut out to be a dad.

03:02.859 --> 03:04.092
Hey, I didn't think I could live

03:04.094 --> 03:05.460
in a Malibu beach house
for free,

03:05.462 --> 03:07.796
but I figured it out.

03:07.798 --> 03:10.432
Well, I don't know
if I can figure this out.

03:10.434 --> 03:12.133
I mean, Th-this kid
has bounced around

03:12.135 --> 03:14.469
the foster care system
his whole life.

03:14.471 --> 03:16.304
I mean, I-I don't know
what he needs.

03:16.306 --> 03:17.606
I mean, does he need structure?

03:17.608 --> 03:18.640
Does he need freedom?

03:18.642 --> 03:21.509
Does he need medication?

03:21.511 --> 03:25.146
I should have asked that
before they dropped him off.

03:25.148 --> 03:27.449
All he needs is
your love and support.

03:27.451 --> 03:29.017
(imitates Alan mockingly)

03:29.019 --> 03:30.719
That's a bunch of crap.

03:30.721 --> 03:33.088
Walden, every parent goes
through this.

03:33.090 --> 03:35.123
B-But you're actually
doing a great job.

03:35.125 --> 03:38.126
You're just overwhelmed
because this is all so new,

03:38.128 --> 03:40.428
a-and you're trying to be
everything to him all the time.

03:40.430 --> 03:42.097
You know, full-time dad,
full-time playmate.

03:42.099 --> 03:43.698
You have to give
yourself a break.

03:43.700 --> 03:44.766
How?

03:44.768 --> 03:46.101
He's 24-7.

03:46.103 --> 03:48.670
He's like the Energizer bunny.

03:48.672 --> 03:51.006
You know why you never met
the Energizer bunny's dad?

03:51.008 --> 03:53.141
'Cause one night,
he went out for cigarettes,

03:53.143 --> 03:56.678
and he just kept going
and going and going.

03:56.680 --> 04:00.348
One thing that'll help
is getting Louis some friends.

04:00.350 --> 04:01.416
Playdates.

04:01.418 --> 04:02.951
They chase each other
around for hours,

04:02.953 --> 04:04.986
eventually they pass out
like work dogs.

04:04.988 --> 04:07.255
Kid'll be in
bed by 8:00,

04:07.257 --> 04:08.890
then it's you, me,
a bowl of popcorn

04:08.892 --> 04:10.992
and binge-watching
&lt;i>The Good Wife.&lt;/i>

04:10.994 --> 04:12.661
Okay, so what?

04:12.663 --> 04:14.596
So, I just...
I'll just Google a place

04:14.598 --> 04:16.831
to meet a fun
cute six-year-old.

04:16.833 --> 04:18.366
Oh, yeah. No.

04:18.368 --> 04:20.902
I heard it when I said it.

04:20.904 --> 04:23.571
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

04:23.573 --> 04:25.340
Uh, this place
is awesome.

04:25.342 --> 04:27.375
They have a rock wall.

04:27.377 --> 04:29.244
Will you climb it with me?

04:29.246 --> 04:32.747
Oh, buddy, you know, the whole
idea is for you to come here

04:32.749 --> 04:34.249
and meet all these
other kids.

04:34.251 --> 04:35.517
No, just you and me.

04:35.519 --> 04:36.718
Please?

04:36.720 --> 04:37.619
Oh.

04:37.621 --> 04:40.088
All right,
I mean, come on.

04:40.090 --> 04:41.523
How do you say no to those eyes?

04:41.525 --> 04:42.724
I hear ya.

04:42.726 --> 04:44.726
Oh, uh, hey, can I have
some money for the snack bar?

04:44.728 --> 04:46.361
Please?
No.

04:46.363 --> 04:49.030
It's not my fault you already
spent all your allowance.

04:55.538 --> 04:57.272
Room for one more?

04:57.274 --> 04:58.440
Absolutely.

04:58.442 --> 04:59.641
Care for a juice box?

04:59.643 --> 05:02.577
We have cherry, grape
and Chardonnay.

05:02.579 --> 05:06.114
Well, what else can I say
except, "chardonn-yay."

05:06.116 --> 05:08.416
Uh, I am Alan.

05:08.418 --> 05:10.485
Uh, that's Louis over there,
he's mine.

05:10.487 --> 05:12.854
I'm Danielle, and that's
my daughter in the water wings.

05:12.856 --> 05:14.989
Oh, is there a pool here?
No.

05:14.991 --> 05:17.592
At some point,
you just pick your battles.

05:18.661 --> 05:20.562
I'm Laurel, this is Julie.

05:21.864 --> 05:24.265
Oh, hot dad on the rock wall.

05:24.267 --> 05:27.369
I claim this
as Mount Louis!

05:28.738 --> 05:30.138
Wow, he's really cute.

05:30.140 --> 05:31.306
Big time.

05:31.308 --> 05:32.574
Sorry, ladies.

05:32.576 --> 05:33.742
He's taken.

05:33.744 --> 05:34.776
No kidding?

05:34.778 --> 05:35.844
Good for you.

05:35.846 --> 05:37.345
How'd you snag him?

05:37.347 --> 05:40.482
I met him at a low point in his
life, and I took care of him.

05:40.484 --> 05:42.484
And he's been taking care
of me every day since.

05:42.486 --> 05:44.986
(oohing, giggling)

05:44.988 --> 05:46.688
That's the kind of man I need.

05:46.690 --> 05:48.790
No, that's the kind
of man I need.

05:48.792 --> 05:49.924
You're married.

05:49.926 --> 05:51.526
Yeah, to Roger.

05:51.528 --> 05:53.495
He hasn't screwed me
since the prenup.

05:53.497 --> 05:55.363
BOTH:
Classic Julie.

05:55.365 --> 05:58.933
Oh, this is so &lt;i>Sex and the City&lt;/i>
right now.

05:58.935 --> 06:01.136
Alan, do we
have any wipes?

06:01.138 --> 06:03.471
The kid above me dripped
something on my face.

06:03.473 --> 06:05.740
The best-case scenario is snot.

06:05.742 --> 06:06.975
Here, I've got some.

06:06.977 --> 06:08.910
Oh, thank you.

06:08.912 --> 06:11.312
Walden, this is, uh,
Laurel, Danielle and Julie.

06:11.314 --> 06:12.847
The ladies, the gals.

06:12.849 --> 06:14.616
The juice box heroes.

06:14.618 --> 06:15.550
Hi.

06:15.552 --> 06:16.484
Hello.

06:16.486 --> 06:17.952
Hi, nice to meet you all.

06:17.954 --> 06:19.320
Your son is adorable.

06:19.322 --> 06:22.190
I'm his husband, silly.

06:22.192 --> 06:23.691
So, uh, which one's yours?

06:23.693 --> 06:24.759
My daughter, Lily,

06:24.761 --> 06:26.628
is the one licking
that little boy.

06:26.630 --> 06:29.097
Sweetie, we don't
lick strangers!

06:29.099 --> 06:31.499
Oh, and I thought
we were gonna be friends.

06:31.501 --> 06:32.967
All right.

06:32.969 --> 06:35.370
I'm headed to the ball pit.

06:35.372 --> 06:38.440
Same thing he said as he dove
under the covers last night.

06:38.442 --> 06:39.841
Boing.

06:41.877 --> 06:44.479
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

06:44.481 --> 06:45.747
Thanks for having us.

06:45.749 --> 06:48.983
I got to say, this is a
great spot for a playdate.

06:48.985 --> 06:50.685
This view is amazing.

06:50.687 --> 06:53.788
Yes. Yes, it is.

06:53.790 --> 06:55.757
You know, I used to walk
by houses like this

06:55.759 --> 06:57.258
and think the people
on the decks were just looking

06:57.260 --> 07:00.361
down their noses at everyone,
feeling all superior.

07:00.363 --> 07:02.063
Now I know it's true.

07:03.132 --> 07:04.599
Roger sold our beach house

07:04.601 --> 07:06.067
'cause he said we never used it.

07:06.069 --> 07:08.736
Using that logic,
we should sell his penis.

07:08.738 --> 07:10.705
(laughs)

07:10.707 --> 07:12.640
Classic Julie.

07:12.642 --> 07:14.909
Hey, w-we should make
this a regular thing.

07:14.911 --> 07:16.578
(thudding, shattering)

07:16.580 --> 07:19.247
Oh. Yeah, next time we'll
do it at one of your houses.

07:20.382 --> 07:22.417
Hey, uh, Louis, is
everything okay?

07:22.419 --> 07:23.852
Over.

07:23.854 --> 07:26.921
LOUIS:
Lego tower fell over.

07:26.923 --> 07:28.590
Uh, you didn't
say "over."

07:28.592 --> 07:30.291
Over.

07:30.293 --> 07:32.260
I said the Lego tower fell over.

07:32.262 --> 07:33.361
Over.

07:33.363 --> 07:35.997
You're so good
with him. Over.

07:35.999 --> 07:39.734
Actually, I-I feel like I
have no idea what I'm doing.

07:39.736 --> 07:41.069
Join the club.

07:41.071 --> 07:42.871
Parenting's
like a yoga class.

07:42.873 --> 07:44.539
You just do what
everybody else is doing

07:44.541 --> 07:46.407
and try not to laugh
when someone farts.

07:49.211 --> 07:52.046
Okay, so all the kids are
playing in Louis' room.

07:52.048 --> 07:54.048
Well, technically, three
of them are playing together,

07:54.050 --> 07:56.484
and Louis is in the corner,
coloring by himself.

07:56.486 --> 07:57.519
That's perfectly normal.

07:57.521 --> 07:59.888
The parenting books call it
"parallel play."

07:59.890 --> 08:01.789
Oh, that's good
to know.

08:01.791 --> 08:03.658
So, in high school,
I wasn't such a weirdo.

08:03.660 --> 08:06.594
I was just a parallel player.

08:06.596 --> 08:09.597
My sex life with my first wife
was a lot of parallel play.

08:10.599 --> 08:11.733
Just give Louis time.

08:11.735 --> 08:13.368
Remember, this is
all new for him.

08:13.370 --> 08:14.836
Kind of like
learning on my honeymoon

08:14.838 --> 08:17.272
that I wasn't going to have sex
was all new for me.

08:17.274 --> 08:19.240
You know, I just want him
to have friends.

08:19.242 --> 08:21.809
You know, like a couple girls,
and a couple boys.

08:21.811 --> 08:23.011
He's gonna be fine.

08:23.013 --> 08:25.079
In the meantime,
&lt;i>I&lt;/i> have made some friends

08:25.081 --> 08:27.715
who have welcomed me
into the secret world of women.

08:27.717 --> 08:29.717
I am this close to discovering
everything about them.

08:29.719 --> 08:31.986
What they like, what
they don't like.

08:31.988 --> 08:34.322
And where they don't like it.

08:34.324 --> 08:37.292
We're supposed to be here
helping Louis make friends.

08:37.294 --> 08:38.993
Oh, please, I see
how you look at Laurel.

08:38.995 --> 08:41.529
It's the same way I look at
a five dollar bill in a tip jar

08:41.531 --> 08:43.298
I think I can swap out
for a single.

08:43.300 --> 08:45.366
Okay, what are you
talking about?

08:45.368 --> 08:47.502
That is Louis'
friend's mom.

08:47.504 --> 08:49.704
And, yes,
we get along great.

08:49.706 --> 08:51.506
And, yes,
she's pretty and nice.

08:51.508 --> 08:53.675
And, yes, she used to be
a gymnast and can still

08:53.677 --> 08:54.809
put her legs
behind her head.

08:54.811 --> 08:55.977
And she is out there.

08:55.979 --> 08:58.980
So why am I still standing here,
talking to you?

08:58.982 --> 09:02.183
I can put my legs behind my
head, but you'll never see it.

09:04.153 --> 09:06.154
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

09:06.156 --> 09:07.655
He was a really nice guy,
Mm-hmm.

09:07.657 --> 09:09.123
and I liked hanging
out with him,

09:09.125 --> 09:10.625
but when we got
to the bedroom,

09:10.627 --> 09:12.627
he was just, well...

09:12.629 --> 09:15.763
If he were a candy bar,
he'd be the fun size.

09:15.765 --> 09:17.665
There's nothing fun
about that.

09:17.667 --> 09:21.202
Yeah, nothing worse
than a small penis.

09:21.204 --> 09:23.471
But, seriously, how
small is too small?

09:24.640 --> 09:25.907
Alan, you are a riot.

09:25.909 --> 09:27.976
We should hang out
with you more often.

09:27.978 --> 09:30.111
Hey, what do you
say, we all go out

09:30.113 --> 09:31.512
this Saturday for
a girls night?

09:31.514 --> 09:33.548
You know, get a limo,
go out dancing,

09:33.550 --> 09:34.916
wear our sluttiest outfits.

09:34.918 --> 09:37.652
Julie, you can wear what
you're wearing now.

09:37.654 --> 09:40.088
Uh, I'm bad.

09:40.090 --> 09:42.156
Should we go check
on the kids?

09:42.158 --> 09:43.591
Are you kidding?

09:43.593 --> 09:46.628
They're set up with pizza,
popsicles and &lt;i>The Lego Movie.&lt;/i>

09:46.630 --> 09:47.862
For the next two hours,

09:47.864 --> 09:49.864
♪ Everything is awesome. ♪

09:49.866 --> 09:52.800
Yeah, I've seen that
movie, like, five times.

09:52.802 --> 09:55.303
I should really watch it
with Louis at some point.

09:55.305 --> 09:56.571
I haven't seen a movie

09:56.573 --> 09:59.240
that wasn't for a kid
in forever.

09:59.242 --> 10:01.242
The other night
I actually had a sex dream

10:01.244 --> 10:02.844
about an animated character.

10:02.846 --> 10:05.346
Whoa...

10:05.348 --> 10:06.280
Prince Charming?

10:06.282 --> 10:09.250
The old guy from &lt;i>Up.&lt;/i>

10:11.286 --> 10:14.355
And, sadly, it was the only sex
I've had in two years.

10:14.357 --> 10:16.691
Well, if it meant a
whole night's sleep,

10:16.693 --> 10:20.395
I'd have sex with an
animated Ed Asner, too.

10:20.397 --> 10:21.863
You think you're tired now.

10:21.865 --> 10:23.798
You missed the hardest years.

10:23.800 --> 10:26.968
The-the... the picky eating,
the tantrums, the bed-wetting.

10:26.970 --> 10:30.304
Okay, to be fair, I get
all of that with Alan.

10:31.674 --> 10:33.975
You guys are a great team.
Hmm.

10:33.977 --> 10:35.710
The only thing
my ex would help with

10:35.712 --> 10:37.578
was driving the babysitter home.

10:37.580 --> 10:39.313
She'd have the kids
in bed by 8:00

10:39.315 --> 10:41.349
and my husband in bed by 10:00.

10:41.351 --> 10:44.018
Oh... that's horrible.

10:44.020 --> 10:45.720
Is she a good sitter?
'Cause we're looking.

10:45.722 --> 10:47.655
Sorry.

10:47.657 --> 10:50.558
Without that jerk of an ex,

10:50.560 --> 10:51.959
I wouldn't have Lily,

10:51.961 --> 10:54.262
and even at six years old,
she's my best friend.

10:54.264 --> 10:56.664
I hope I get there
with Louis at some point.

10:56.666 --> 10:58.099
You'll get there.

10:58.101 --> 10:59.634
I hope I stay there with Lily.

10:59.636 --> 11:01.436
I'm afraid that by the time
she's a teenager,

11:01.438 --> 11:03.171
she'll be like,
"Mom, you're 100!

11:03.173 --> 11:05.273
Nobody believes
I'm your sister!"

11:05.275 --> 11:07.241
Okay, how could anyone say that

11:07.243 --> 11:10.745
about someone as pretty,
smart and flexible as you?

11:10.747 --> 11:12.413
(laughs)

11:12.415 --> 11:13.981
You're so sweet.

11:13.983 --> 11:15.583
You don't happen to know

11:15.585 --> 11:18.352
of a single, straight version
of you, do you?

11:18.354 --> 11:21.022
I used to know one.

11:21.024 --> 11:22.990
Are you looking for a date?

11:22.992 --> 11:25.426
I told you,
it's been over two years.

11:25.428 --> 11:27.628
I need a lot more than a date.

11:34.002 --> 11:36.571
♪ Popsicles are awesome! ♪

11:37.673 --> 11:40.241
Okay, I'm gonna go
check on the kids.

11:40.243 --> 11:43.044
I'm gonna wait
here for a bit.

11:43.046 --> 11:44.946
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

11:51.657 --> 11:53.290
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

11:53.292 --> 11:54.625
Hope you are ready to go.

11:54.627 --> 11:55.860
The ladies just Instagrammed

11:55.862 --> 11:57.395
a selfie
from the limo.

11:57.397 --> 12:00.431
#GirlsNightOut
is on like Chaka Khan!

12:00.433 --> 12:03.100
All right, Louis
is eating his dinner.

12:03.102 --> 12:04.201
WALDEN:
Oh, great. Chaka Khan!

12:04.203 --> 12:07.004
Hey, thank you again
for watching him tonight.

12:07.006 --> 12:08.539
And if anything
comes up--

12:08.541 --> 12:10.341
and I mean anything at all--
you call my cell.

12:10.343 --> 12:11.308
Got it.

12:11.310 --> 12:13.277
Oh, if he wants to play a game,

12:13.279 --> 12:14.712
he likes Chutes and Ladders.

12:14.714 --> 12:16.180
And if he want
to watch a cartoon,

12:16.182 --> 12:17.648
he likes &lt;i>Phineas and Ferb.&lt;/i>

12:17.650 --> 12:21.052
And who does he like in the
Cardinals-Rams game tonight?

12:21.054 --> 12:22.620
I know I'm being
a little bit crazy,

12:22.622 --> 12:24.455
but this is the first time
I've left him alone.

12:24.457 --> 12:26.824
Relax, I had five kids,

12:26.826 --> 12:29.727
12 grandkids and
four great-grandkids.

12:29.729 --> 12:31.896
I've done it all.

12:31.898 --> 12:35.566
Except teach them
about birth control.

12:35.568 --> 12:37.635
I don't feel good.

12:37.637 --> 12:39.503
Oh, no.
What's the matter?

12:39.505 --> 12:40.871
I just threw up.

12:40.873 --> 12:43.641
Oh, no.
Oh... yep.

12:43.643 --> 12:45.342
He's got a fever.
(sighs)

12:45.344 --> 12:47.211
I'll bet it was that snot-nosed kid
on the rock wall.

12:47.213 --> 12:49.280
Typhoid Tyler.
Yeah.

12:49.282 --> 12:50.681
I got this.

12:50.683 --> 12:53.384
I worked for Charlie
for ten years.

12:53.386 --> 12:55.920
I know vomit.

12:55.922 --> 12:59.190
Cleaning it up
and inducing it.

12:59.192 --> 13:01.692
I never threw up
SpaghettiOs before.

13:01.694 --> 13:03.394
It's kind of fun.
Oh...

13:03.396 --> 13:04.695
(Berta laughs)

13:04.697 --> 13:06.030
Should we go
to the doctor?

13:06.032 --> 13:07.064
Oh, no, no.

13:07.066 --> 13:08.632
I'm sure it's
just a tummy ache.

13:08.634 --> 13:10.434
I'll text the girls and let 'em know
we can't make it.

13:10.436 --> 13:12.436
Oh, no. Come on.
You go.

13:12.438 --> 13:13.771
You sure?

13:13.773 --> 13:15.806
Yeah, come on, this is
what a parent does.

13:15.808 --> 13:17.141
This is what I
signed up for.

13:17.143 --> 13:18.309
Besides, you took
a half an hour

13:18.311 --> 13:20.077
getting into
those Spanx.

13:21.213 --> 13:23.147
All right. Sorry.

13:23.149 --> 13:24.882
Um... I'll send
pictures.

13:24.884 --> 13:26.417
Danielle said that
if I get her drunk enough

13:26.419 --> 13:27.685
she'll show me her tattoos.

13:27.687 --> 13:31.055
Uh, she's got a bird on her hand
and two in her...

13:31.057 --> 13:34.091
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

13:34.093 --> 13:35.726
Walden...

13:35.728 --> 13:37.328
I'm sorry I got sick.

13:37.330 --> 13:38.796
What? Come on, man.

13:38.798 --> 13:39.730
Don't be sorry.

13:39.732 --> 13:40.798
It happens.

13:40.800 --> 13:42.366
&lt;i>I'm&lt;/i> sorry you don't feel well.

13:42.368 --> 13:44.435
But you were going
to go out with Alan

13:44.437 --> 13:46.036
and now you can't 'cause of me.

13:46.038 --> 13:48.038
Oh, I'm not missing anything.

13:48.040 --> 13:50.241
You ever seen Alan dance?

13:52.477 --> 13:53.477
All right.

13:53.479 --> 13:54.912
Now, you get some good sleep

13:54.914 --> 13:57.181
and I'm gonna be right here

13:57.183 --> 13:58.315
if you need anything.

13:58.317 --> 13:59.950
Oh, and you know
who else'll be here?

13:59.952 --> 14:02.219
Your new friend,
"Barfy the Bucket."

14:03.488 --> 14:05.089
(high-pitched voice):
♪ I'm here for you ♪

14:05.091 --> 14:07.725
♪ If you're ready to spew! ♪

14:07.727 --> 14:09.627
(laughs)

14:09.629 --> 14:11.195
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

14:11.197 --> 14:13.364
(doorbell rings)

14:17.536 --> 14:18.536
Hey.

14:18.538 --> 14:19.770
Laurel.

14:19.772 --> 14:21.038
What are you
doing here?

14:21.040 --> 14:22.306
I bailed.

14:22.308 --> 14:23.808
Didn't Alan tell you?

14:23.810 --> 14:25.509
No, the only
thing I got

14:25.511 --> 14:27.411
was a picture of
Alan twerking.

14:28.947 --> 14:33.484
With a caption that said,
"Alan got his groove back."

14:33.486 --> 14:35.619
Well, when I heard
that Louis was sick,

14:35.621 --> 14:37.188
I thought you could
use some help.

14:37.190 --> 14:38.355
And soup.

14:38.357 --> 14:39.723
Come on, that
is so sweet.

14:39.725 --> 14:41.525
You did not
have to do this.

14:41.527 --> 14:43.994
You look amazing.
Oh, thanks.

14:43.996 --> 14:45.596
Well, I already had
the sitter, and...

14:45.598 --> 14:48.666
first rule of parenting:
Never cancel the sitter.

14:48.668 --> 14:50.835
Well, unless she's banging
your husband.

14:52.370 --> 14:53.103
Too far?

14:53.105 --> 14:54.972
No, uh, "too far"

14:54.974 --> 14:56.407
was starting a Facebook page

14:56.409 --> 14:59.910
called "Tiffany Jones is a
Husband-Stealing Little Bitch."

15:01.546 --> 15:04.281
Uh, do you know what Louis has?

15:04.283 --> 15:05.783
Uh, well, I went on the Internet

15:05.785 --> 15:08.018
and I've narrowed it down
to either the flu,

15:08.020 --> 15:11.121
rickets
or early-onset menopause.

15:11.123 --> 15:12.523
Second rule of parenting:

15:12.525 --> 15:14.024
Never consult the Internet.

15:14.026 --> 15:15.593
(chuckles)
How's he doing now?

15:15.595 --> 15:17.461
Well, he's asleep

15:17.463 --> 15:18.729
and he's doing
pretty well.

15:18.731 --> 15:20.364
Oh, good, because...

15:20.366 --> 15:22.933
I brought this for us.

15:22.935 --> 15:23.901
Oh...

15:23.903 --> 15:25.636
You know,
third rule of parenting:

15:25.638 --> 15:28.505
Kids aren't the only ones
that can drink from a bottle.

15:28.507 --> 15:30.841
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

15:30.843 --> 15:32.576
♪ Oh, yes, it's ladies' night ♪

15:32.578 --> 15:34.445
♪ And the feeling's right ♪

15:34.447 --> 15:37.147
♪ Oh, yes, it's ladies' night,
oh, what a night ♪

15:37.149 --> 15:39.783
(deep voice):
♪ Oh, what a night. ♪

15:39.785 --> 15:41.552
(whooping)

15:41.554 --> 15:42.554
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

15:42.555 --> 15:43.687
Easy, there.

15:43.689 --> 15:45.122
I pour strong when
the alcohol's free.

15:45.124 --> 15:46.323
I have to cram a lot of fun

15:46.325 --> 15:47.825
into a short amount of time.
ALAN: Mmm.

15:47.827 --> 15:49.493
Kind of like sex with Roger.

15:49.495 --> 15:50.661
(women laughing)

15:50.663 --> 15:52.096
What is it with guys

15:52.098 --> 15:53.697
and their constant need for sex?

15:53.699 --> 15:55.699
Look at Alan here.
He's out with two women,

15:55.701 --> 15:57.568
but I bet even he
wants sex right now.

15:57.570 --> 15:59.803
I do. I really do.

15:59.805 --> 16:01.105
Oh, my God!
Let's dance!

16:01.107 --> 16:02.239
(whoops)

16:02.241 --> 16:03.574
(both whooping)

16:03.576 --> 16:05.242
♪ ♪

16:05.244 --> 16:06.644
Come up here, Alan!

16:06.646 --> 16:08.812
No, I-I'm good down here.

16:10.181 --> 16:11.448
Well, he's still asleep

16:11.450 --> 16:13.217
and he feels cooler,

16:13.219 --> 16:15.019
but now I'm worried that
he might have hypothermia.

16:15.021 --> 16:16.520
Yeah.

16:16.522 --> 16:18.022
You know, one of
the hardest lessons

16:18.024 --> 16:19.690
I've had to learn as a parent
is sometimes

16:19.692 --> 16:21.125
you just
gotta relax.

16:21.127 --> 16:22.259
(laughing):
Relax?

16:22.261 --> 16:23.627
All I do is worry.

16:23.629 --> 16:24.762
And now that
I don't sleep,

16:24.764 --> 16:26.397
I have plenty
of time to do it.

16:26.399 --> 16:28.299
Is he exercising enough?

16:28.301 --> 16:30.501
Is he eating right?
Does he even want to stay here?

16:30.503 --> 16:33.137
I mean, this is the most
terrifying thing I've ever done.

16:33.139 --> 16:35.606
And-- this is scarier than
when I bought the big iPhone

16:35.608 --> 16:37.675
and I didn't know
if it would fit in my pocket.

16:37.677 --> 16:39.643
(laughs)

16:41.780 --> 16:43.347
You think
you're scared?

16:43.349 --> 16:44.615
I have a daughter.

16:44.617 --> 16:46.650
I worry about
all the same things you do,

16:46.652 --> 16:48.218
plus penises.

16:48.220 --> 16:49.853
And with you,

16:49.855 --> 16:51.956
you have to worry
about animated penises.

16:53.625 --> 16:55.259
I should have never
told you that.

16:55.261 --> 16:57.261
You should never
tell anyone that.

16:57.263 --> 16:59.797
All right, all right.
What-what's your next date?

16:59.799 --> 17:01.231
Shrek?

17:02.567 --> 17:04.735
No, no, no.
The-the genie from &lt;i>Aladdin.&lt;/i>

17:04.737 --> 17:06.203
Or-or maybe you'll
have a three-way

17:06.205 --> 17:08.505
with the Hakuna Matata guys?

17:09.841 --> 17:11.208
Shut up.

17:11.210 --> 17:12.210
Make me.

17:12.211 --> 17:14.745
I could make you.

17:14.747 --> 17:16.480
Oh, yeah?

17:16.482 --> 17:17.815
Mm-hmm.

17:17.817 --> 17:19.550
I'm right here.

17:25.390 --> 17:28.225
I'm so sorry.
What? Why?

17:30.628 --> 17:32.396
You're married.

17:32.398 --> 17:34.565
To a man.
Oh...

17:34.567 --> 17:35.799
That. Uh...

17:35.801 --> 17:36.934
I should go.

17:36.936 --> 17:39.370
No, no, no, no. No, no, wait,
wait, wait, wait.

17:39.372 --> 17:42.139
Here's... okay, the thing
about my marriage is...

17:42.141 --> 17:43.807
I'm not gay.

17:43.809 --> 17:46.010
Does Alan know?

17:47.178 --> 17:49.313
His brain knows,

17:49.315 --> 17:52.349
but his heart may not.

17:52.351 --> 17:53.617
Here-here-here,
here's the thing.

17:53.619 --> 17:54.952
Here's the thing:
Alan is...

17:54.954 --> 17:56.253
he's my best
friend, okay?

17:56.255 --> 17:57.788
And-and he married me
as a favor

17:57.790 --> 18:00.290
so it would be easier
to adopt Louis.

18:00.292 --> 18:01.292
Okay? And-and...

18:01.293 --> 18:03.293
Well, I mean...
the fact that you

18:03.295 --> 18:04.295
married your
best friend

18:04.296 --> 18:06.897
so that you could
adopt Louis is..

18:06.899 --> 18:09.299
actually
very sweet.

18:09.301 --> 18:11.969
So...

18:14.372 --> 18:16.273
...you're not
mad at me?

18:16.275 --> 18:18.742
Hakuna matata.

18:20.278 --> 18:23.113
That's my philosophy.

18:25.550 --> 18:27.851
So...

18:29.154 --> 18:31.188
...can we kiss again?
Yeah.

18:33.091 --> 18:35.169
It's been so long since
I've kissed a man.

18:35.170 --> 18:35.727
Oh...

18:35.728 --> 18:37.895
I wish I could say
the same thing.

18:38.797 --> 18:41.999
Julie, your boobs look
great in that blouse.

18:42.001 --> 18:43.367
I am so jealous.

18:43.369 --> 18:44.802
Thanks to my kids,

18:44.804 --> 18:47.604
mine went from 34B
to 34 "used to be."

18:47.606 --> 18:49.440
I like your boobs.

18:49.442 --> 18:50.274
I don't know.

18:50.276 --> 18:51.508
What do you think, Alan,

18:51.510 --> 18:52.843
should I get 'em done?

18:52.845 --> 18:54.244
Oh, well, I'm no expert.

18:54.246 --> 18:55.412
I-I think they're lovely.

18:55.414 --> 18:56.814
Are you sure?

18:56.816 --> 18:57.948
Oh, my!

18:57.950 --> 18:59.716
You just did that.

18:59.718 --> 19:02.052
Um, you guys, I-I think there's
something I should tell you...

19:02.054 --> 19:03.287
He has nothing
to compare them with.

19:03.289 --> 19:04.488
Here.

19:07.125 --> 19:09.726
You guys are my best friends.

19:09.728 --> 19:10.961
Aw!
Aw!

19:10.963 --> 19:13.030
Okay, okay.

19:13.032 --> 19:15.232
I-I know you haven't
done this in a while,

19:15.234 --> 19:17.201
so I don't want
to go too fast,

19:17.203 --> 19:18.836
but do you want
to go up to my...

19:18.838 --> 19:19.670
Let's go.

19:19.672 --> 19:21.939
Oh.

19:21.941 --> 19:24.741
LOUIS (over walkie-talkie):
Walden?

19:24.743 --> 19:26.310
Can you come here?

19:27.645 --> 19:29.980
He didn't say "over,"
so it doesn't count.

19:31.249 --> 19:32.649
Oh, go check on him.

19:32.651 --> 19:34.017
It's fine.

19:34.019 --> 19:36.086
I've waited for two years,
I can wait a little bit longer.

19:36.088 --> 19:39.022
Thank you.

19:39.024 --> 19:42.025
Oh. Don't start without me.

19:42.027 --> 19:43.727
Or do.

19:43.729 --> 19:46.063
Oh, uh, by the way,
if you want to stay in the mood,

19:46.065 --> 19:48.232
we get all the cartoon channels.

19:50.535 --> 19:52.836
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:04.883 --> 20:06.550
Walden?

20:15.860 --> 20:17.494
Parenting rule number four:

20:17.496 --> 20:19.596
Sleep is better than sex.

20:19.598 --> 20:21.198
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:27.525 --> 20:29.926
This is the best night
of my life.

20:29.928 --> 20:32.195
I love you girls.

20:32.197 --> 20:34.931
We should get matching tattoos.

20:34.933 --> 20:36.533
I have a better idea.

20:36.535 --> 20:37.767
Let's go to a strip club!

20:37.769 --> 20:40.337
That is better!

20:40.339 --> 20:42.772
(whooping)

20:42.774 --> 20:45.642
♪ Oh, yes,
it's ladies' night... ♪

20:47.645 --> 20:49.846
This was a great idea.

20:51.916 --> 20:54.884
That is definitely
bigger than fun size.

20:54.886 --> 20:56.386
Make it rain!

20:56.388 --> 20:58.321
Yeah, give him
some money!

20:59.123 --> 21:01.991
Oh, this just keeps
getting better.

21:03.639 --> 21:10.139
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>
